SUMMARY:Japanese Tea Gathering: Shiwasu - Friday
DESCRIPTION:Join tea master Chizuko Sueyoshi and members of the Japanese Tea Practitioners of Durham for a moment of respite in the Duke Gardens teahouse\, where you will experience the centering calm of a Japanese tea gathering in the Urasenke tradition. Enjoy the aesthetics\, poetry and serenity of this rich tradition over an enticing bowl of whisked green tea and a Japanese confection.  Guests will be escorted on a 15-minute walk to the teahouse\, where seating is on the floor unless a chair is requested upon registration by emailing GardensEducation@duke.edu. For ages 12 and up. \nFee: $68; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Fees apply \nLocation: Onsite at Duke Gardens. \nAccessibility: This is a small group program that takes place indoors in a non-climate controlled space with floor seating\, in a location that requires outdoors traveling on a combination of paved and unpaved paths with some uneven surfaces and moderate inclines.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/japanese-tea-gathering-shiwasu-friday/
LOCATION:Onsite at Duke Gardens – directions to follow
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs,Tea Ceremony
